//? Title: RevNet: Reconstructed Activations and Measured Memory
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Additive coupling lets most residual-unit inputs be recovered from outputs. We verify
nontrivial inverses, compare every gradient against ordinary backpropagation, measure live tensor
memory across depths, then explicitly train the full RevNet-38 with reversible tensor Adam updates.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.3_residual_and_dense_families/revnet.cpp`.

> The method

Split the channel axis into equal halves. An invertible unit computes

$$y_1=x_1+F(x_2),\qquad y_2=x_2+G(y_1),\qquad
 x_2=y_2-G(y_1),\qquad x_1=y_1-F(x_2).$$
\alttext(The additive coupling can reconstruct inputs without inverting the learned F or G functions.)

F/G need not themselves be invertible. They are deterministic preactivated basic two-3×3
functions or bottlenecks with 1×1/3×3/1×1 and inner width one quarter of their output.
There is no post-addition ReLU. Learned-scale BN uses epsilon .001; the first F after the
stem skips BN/ReLU. Basic dimension-changing shortcuts average-pool and symmetrically zero-pad
half-maps; bottleneck shortcuts use raw bias-free 1×1 projections. Stage-entry units are stored,
including the first-F exception. They cannot use the ordinary equal-width inverse.

The stem is 3×3 conv/BN/ReLU for CIFAR or 7×7/2 conv/BN/ReLU plus SAME max-pool for
ImageNet. The head concatenates halves, applies BN/ReLU, global mean and a linear classifier.
He-uniform fan-in replaces the release's truncated-normal fan-out initialization. Full learned
counts are 464890/1729194/1748778 for CIFAR-38/110/164 and 27553128/45428072 for
ImageNet-56/104. Count-only ImageNet forwards use 64 pixels; the parameter budgets do not
depend on spatial size. No pretrained weights, dropout or hidden fitting occurs.

Ordinary mode stores normal autograd activations. Stored-input mode checkpoints every unit
and recomputes from its retained input; reversible mode checkpoints stage entries and reconstructs
interior inputs from outputs using nn::reversible_sequence. Both suppress repeated BN moving
updates during backward. The context borrows parameter/state stores: they must outlive backward
and weights must remain unchanged between forward and backward. Float32 reconstruction introduces
drift and can move early-unit gradients; compare every tensor against ordinary gradients rather
than assuming exact equivalence. The diagnostic reports worst relative L2 errors and checks
stored-input error <=1e-6, reconstructed-gradient error <=.05 and input drift <=1e-4.

Memory measurements warm each model, then track one forward/gradient step above its parameter,
state and data baseline, using batch 16 at 32 pixels. All three modes share widths; stage lengths
are 3/9/18. The exact logical tensor-buffer counter includes temporary/gradient tensors and excludes
allocator overhead, process RSS and optimizer state. It is not a runtime benchmark. Recomputation
saves activation storage by performing extra forward arithmetic; parameter storage still grows.

The visible Adam loop trains full-width/depth RevNet-38, selecting reversible backward explicitly
for every training forward. Seven batch-eight epochs use 128 fit/64 validation/64 official-test
images, Adam(.001), explicit kernel L2=.0001/2 and independent padded crops/flips. Validation
selects paired learned/moving-state checkpoints before test evaluation. This bounded run differs
from the original larger source fit and the paper's long SGD schedule; it is not a benchmark.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/revnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/revnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/revnet_concept.tikz > build/revnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/revnet_concept.svg build/revnet_concept.dvi > build/revnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
