3 units/stage, batch 16 at 32 pixels: ordinary 46.797 MiB, reversible 22.164 MiB, stored-input 22.111 MiB, ordinary/reversible 2.111.
9 units/stage, batch 16 at 32 pixels: ordinary 129.316 MiB, reversible 25.822 MiB, stored-input 40.325 MiB, ordinary/reversible 5.008.
18 units/stage, batch 16 at 32 pixels: ordinary 253.095 MiB, reversible 31.308 MiB, stored-input 71.216 MiB, ordinary/reversible 8.084.
\image(figures/revnet_memory.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Measured logical live tensor-buffer peaks above warmed parameters, BN state and input/target tensors. Step gradients and temporary buffers are included. Models keep RevNet-38 widths while units per stage change. These are neither process RSS nor optimizer-step/timing measurements; recomputation trades arithmetic for activation storage.)
\alttext(Measured logical live tensor-buffer peaks above warmed parameters, BN state and input/target tensors. Step gradients and temporary buffers are included. Models keep RevNet-38 widths while units per stage change. These are neither process RSS nor optimizer-step/timing measurements; recomputation trades arithmetic for activation storage.)

In this run, stored-input checkpoint gradients agree exactly at the printed precision.
Reconstruction moves the worst parameter-gradient tensor by relative L2 0.000001338
at depth 38 and 0.006258122 at depth 164; the corresponding maximum input drifts are
0.000000448 and 0.000004861. With 18 units per stage, reversible peak step storage
is 31.308 MiB versus 253.095 MiB for ordinary autograd, a measured ratio of 8.084.
Those figures apply to this fixture, baseline and buffer counter.

> Dataset and reversible fitting

Original CIFAR images precede the full fitting loop; the mode choice is visible in its forward callback.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/revnet_inputs.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("cifar10", (cache / "cifar10").string());

  const auto raw =
      n::data::LoadCifar({cache / "cifar10/data_batch_1.bin"}, n::data::Cifar::k10);
  const auto images = n::cast(raw.images, n::DType::Float32) / 255.;
  const auto labels = raw.labels;

  std::vector<int64_t> rows;
  for (int cls = 0; cls < 10; ++cls) {
    for (int64_t row = 0; row < labels.numel(); ++row)
      if (labels.at({row}) == cls) {
        rows.push_back(row);
        break;
      }
  }
  if (rows.size() != 10)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::take_rows(images, rows), "build/revnet_inputs.png", 5, 0., 1., 4, 1.,
                     4);
  std::print("One original cached training image per class, IDs 0..4 then 5..9.\n");
}
```
